Make the LuaDist CMakeLists configure under CMake 4.

Two problems, both in the first two lines.  cmake_minimum_required asks for
2.8, and CMake 4 refuses to configure any project asking for less than 3.5.
It is also called after project(), which CMake has warned about for years
and which means the policy version is not yet set while project() runs.
3.10 is the oldest release whose policies this file is actually written
against (it uses nothing newer), and the upper bound keeps CMake from
applying policy defaults the 2012 code has never seen.

LuaDist is a dead packaging fork, so there is nobody upstream to send this
to; the tolua++ sources it wraps carry no CMake build of their own.

Upstream: not submitted (LuaDist unmaintained since 2013)
Applies-to: all environments
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index b59ef7c..6115613 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 # For details see the COPYRIGHT file distributed with LuaDist.
 # Please note that the package source code is licensed under its own license.
 
+cmake_minimum_required ( VERSION 3.10...4.0 )
 project ( toluapp C )
-cmake_minimum_required ( VERSION 2.8 )
 include ( cmake/dist.cmake )
 
 find_package ( Lua REQUIRED )
